<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P>Lithium-ion costs dropped 89% since 2010, reaching $139/kWh in 2024. Grid-scale deployments hit 47 GWh globally, with 4-hour duration becoming standard. Sodium-ion and iron-air technologies promise sub-$100/kWh by 2027.</P>
        <P>Grid integration challenges persist as storage penetration exceeds 15% in California and Texas. Frequency regulation and voltage support require sophisticated inverter controls. Interconnection queues stretch 36 months average, limiting deployment velocity despite falling hardware costs.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV data-vertical-align="end">
        <H1 style="text-align: right"><B>Storage solves everything.</B></H1>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>